The speech model used by myna-server-parakeet
=============================================

This package does not contain a model. On the service's first start it
downloads one into ~/.cache/myna/models/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8 from
https://github.com/Kieirra/murmure-model (release 1.2.0), and checks it
against a pinned SHA-256 hash.

That model is NVIDIA's Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3
(https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3), Copyright NVIDIA
Corporation, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC-BY-4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to ONNX and
quantised to int8. No model was retrained. The derived files and their
authors, each also published under CC-BY-4.0:

- decoder_joint-model.int8.onnx, nemo128.onnx, vocab.txt: the ONNX export
  by istupakov, https://huggingface.co/istupakov/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-onnx
- encoder-model.int8.onnx: the SmoothQuant int8 encoder by Olicorne
  (thiswillbeyourgithub),
  https://huggingface.co/Olicorne/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-smoothquant-onnx

The bundle is assembled and released by Kieirra as murmure-model.
This notice is adapted from Myna's parakeet-snap/NOTICE (Canonical Ltd.).
